From 40f426c6c560dedf02d438d85fd5e0e4e7c1e057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ylfeid <261695633+ylfeid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:11:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod: remove non-const i2d_TYPE prototypes
 from SYNOPSIS

Since OpenSSL 3.0 the i2d_TYPE(), i2d_TYPE_fp() and i2d_TYPE_bio()
functions take a const TYPE argument.  The SYNOPSIS still listed
the old non-const prototypes alongside the const ones, so each function
appeared twice.  Drop the stale non-const lines.

Resolves: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/33182
CLA: trivial
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Frederik Wedel-Heinen <fwh.openssl@gmail.com>
Merge-date: Sun Nov  1 15:25:01 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33336
(cherry picked from commit 5331430606c1c6a79ec236337ec04ccaba7da0e6)
---
 doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod b/doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod
index 9f0589a87e4c..2f020fe18f13 100644
--- a/doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod
+++ b/doc/man3/d2i_X509.pod
@@ -453,11 +453,8 @@ i2d_X509_VAL,
  TYPE *d2i_TYPE_fp(FILE *fp, TYPE **a);
 
  int i2d_TYPE(const TYPE *a, unsigned char **ppout);
- int i2d_TYPE(TYPE *a, unsigned char **ppout);
  int i2d_TYPE_fp(FILE *fp, const TYPE *a);
- int i2d_TYPE_fp(FILE *fp, TYPE *a);
  int i2d_TYPE_bio(BIO *bp, const TYPE *a);
- int i2d_TYPE_bio(BIO *bp, TYPE *a);
 
 =head1 DESCRIPTION
 
